# Add New Features to Home Credit Default Risk Pipeline

## Goal

Add 7 new features from the original (`og_application_train.csv` / `og_application_test.csv`) datasets to the existing pipeline, then rewrite all 6 notebooks to reflect the expanded feature set.

### New Features

| # | Original Column | New Column/Transform | Type | Missing (Train) | Missing (Test) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `EXT_SOURCE_1` | `EXT_SOURCE_1` (as-is) | Numerical (float) | 173,378 (~56.4%) | 20,532 (~42.1%) |
| 2 | `EXT_SOURCE_2` | `EXT_SOURCE_2` (as-is) | Numerical (float) | 660 (~0.2%) | 8 |
| 3 | `EXT_SOURCE_3` | `EXT_SOURCE_3` (as-is) | Numerical (float) | 60,965 (~19.8%) | 8,668 (~17.8%) |
| 4 | `DAYS_BIRTH` | → `AGE` = `abs(DAYS_BIRTH) / 365.25` | Numerical (float) | 0 | 0 |
| 5 | `DAYS_EMPLOYED` | → `YEARS_EMPLOYED` = cleaned & converted | Numerical (float) | 0 | 0 |
| 6 | `ORGANIZATION_TYPE` | `ORGANIZATION_TYPE` | Categorical (58 unique) | 0 | 0 |
| 7 | `NAME_HOUSING_TYPE` | `NAME_HOUSING_TYPE` | Categorical (6 unique) | 0 | 0 |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **`DAYS_EMPLOYED` anomaly**: The original data contains a value of `365243` (positive, ~1000 years) for unemployed/retired applicants. This must be replaced with `0` before converting to `YEARS_EMPLOYED = abs(DAYS_EMPLOYED) / 365.25`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **`EXT_SOURCE_1` has 56% missing values**. We will use median imputation (computed from train) for all three EXT_SOURCE columns, since they are the single most predictive features in the Home Credit dataset.

